1
00:04:00,000 --> 00:04:06,000
Believe the unbelievable.

2
00:08:00,000 --> 00:08:06,000
The Matrix is a action, science fiction film directed by Lana Wachowski.

3
00:12:00,000 --> 00:12:06,000
Set in the 22nd century, The Matrix tells the story of a computer hacker who joins a group of
underground insurgents fighting the vast and powerful computers who now rule the earth.

4
00:16:00,000 --> 00:16:06,000
Neo, played by Keanu Reeves.

5
00:20:00,000 --> 00:20:06,000
Morpheus, played by Laurence Fishburne.

6
00:24:00,000 --> 00:24:06,000
Trinity, played by Carrie-Anne Moss.

7
00:28:00,000 --> 00:28:06,000
Agent Smith, played by Hugo Weaving.

8
00:32:00,000 --> 00:32:06,000
Oracle, played by Gloria Foster.

9
00:36:00,000 --> 00:36:06,000
Cypher, played by Joe Pantoliano.

10
00:40:00,000 --> 00:40:06,000
The Matrix is a 1999 science fiction action film
written and directed by the Wachowskis.

11
00:44:00,000 --> 00:44:06,000
The first installment in the Matrix film series, it stars Keanu Reeves, Laurence
Fishburne, Carrie-Anne Moss, Hugo Weaving, and Joe Pantoliano.

12
00:48:00,000 --> 00:48:06,000
It depicts a dystopian future in which humanity is unknowingly trapped inside
the Matrix, a simulated reality created by intelligent machines.

13
00:52:00,000 --> 00:52:06,000
The plot follows the computer hacker Neo, who is recruited by
Morpheus into a rebellion against the machines.

14
00:56:00,000 --> 00:56:06,000
Following the success of the Wachowskis' 1996 film Bound, Warner Bros.

15
01:00:00,000 --> 01:00:06,000
gave the directing duo the go-ahead to make The Matrix.

16
01:04:00,000 --> 01:04:06,000
The film's action scenes were influenced by anime and martial arts films, particularly
fight choreography and wire fu techniques from Hong Kong action cinema.

17
01:08:00,000 --> 01:08:06,000
Other influences include Plato's cave, 1990's Telnet hacker
communities, and William Gibson's cyberpunk novel Neuromancer.

18
01:12:00,000 --> 01:12:06,000
The Matrix popularized terms such as the red pill, as well as a novel visual effect known as "bullet time" in which a character's heightened perception is
represented by allowing the action within a shot to progress in slow motion while the camera appears to move through the scene at normal speed.

19
01:16:00,000 --> 01:16:06,000
The Matrix opened in theaters in the United States on March 31, 1999, to widespread acclaim from critics, who
praised its innovative visual effects, action sequences, cinematography and entertainment value.

20
01:20:00,000 --> 01:20:06,000
The film was a box office success, grossing over
$460 million on a $63 million budget.

21
01:24:00,000 --> 01:24:06,000
It became the highest-grossing Warner Bros.

22
01:28:00,000 --> 01:28:06,000
film of 1999 and the fourth-highest-grossing film of that year.

23
01:32:00,000 --> 01:32:06,000
The Matrix received Academy Awards for Best Visual Effects, Best Film
Editing, Best Sound and Best Sound Effects Editing.

24
01:36:00,000 --> 01:36:06,000
It was also the recipient of numerous other accolades, including Best Sound and
Best Special Visual Effects at the 53rd British Academy Film Awards.

25
01:40:00,000 --> 01:40:06,000
The Wachowskis were awarded Best Director and Best Science
Fiction Film at the 26th Saturn Awards.

26
01:44:00,000 --> 01:44:06,000
The Matrix is considered to be among the greatest
science fiction films of all time.

27
01:48:00,000 --> 01:48:06,000
In 2012, it was selected for preservation in the United States National Film Registry by the
Library of Congress for being "culturally, historically, and aesthetically significant".

28
01:52:00,000 --> 01:52:06,000
The film's success led to two sequels by the Wachowskis, The Matrix
Reloaded and The Matrix Revolutions, both released in 2003.

29
01:56:00,000 --> 01:56:06,000
The Matrix franchise was further expanded through the production of comic
books, video games and an animated anthology film, The Animatrix.

30
02:00:00,000 --> 02:00:06,000
The franchise has also inspired books and theories expanding on some of the
religious and philosophical ideas alluded to in the films.

31
02:04:00,000 --> 02:04:06,000
A fourth film, The Matrix Resurrections, was directed by
Lana Wachowski and was released in 2021.

32
02:08:00,000 --> 02:08:06,000
The film explores themes of man vs machine, martial arts, kung
fu, dreams, artificial intelligence (a.i.).

33
02:12:00,000 --> 02:12:06,000
The tone is thought_provoking.
